{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And YHWH drove an east wind.</b> 'And YHWH' means He and His court. An east wind is ever prepared for punishment: in Egypt it is written, 'and YHWH drove an east wind'; at the sea it is written (Exodus 14:21), 'and YHWH drove the sea with an east wind'; concerning the two tribes it is written (Jeremiah 18:17), 'like an east wind I will scatter them before the enemy'; concerning the ten tribes it is written (Hosea 13:15), 'though he be fruitful among his companions, an east wind shall come, the wind of HaShem coming up from the wilderness, and his spring shall become dry, and his fountain shall be dried up'; at the time of exile it is written (Isaiah 27:8), 'He measureth it by her harsh wind in the day of the east wind'; concerning Tyre it is written (Ezekiel 27:26), 'the east wind has broken you in the heart of the seas'; concerning Jonah it is written (Jonah 4:8), 'and HaShem appointed a vehement east wind'; in the punishment of Gog and Magog it is written (Psalms 48:8), 'with an east wind You break the ships of Tarshish.'" "<b>It was morning, and the east wind lifted the locusts.</b> An east wind brought the punishment, and a west wind removed the punishment, as it is written: 'and HaShem turned a very strong west wind, and it lifted the locusts and drove them into the Sea of Reeds.' And the reason it says 'it was morning' is because the punishment of the wicked is in the morning, and thus Scripture says (Psalms 101:8), 'every morning I will destroy all the wicked of the land,' and Moses mentioned concerning the punishment of Korah (Numbers 16:5), 'in the morning HaShem will show who are His,' and correspondingly we find that the deliverance of the righteous is in the morning, as it is said to Moses (Exodus 34:2), 'and be ready in the morning,' and it is written (Isaiah 33:2), 'be their arm every morning, our salvation also in time of trouble,' and it is written (Lamentations 3:23), 'they are new every morning, great is Your faithfulness.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:35.109647915Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}